'''Saw Gerrera's camp''',<ref name="Replacements">{{TBB|Replacements}}</ref> also known as the '''Onderon insurgent camp''', was a secret base of operations used by the [[Onderon rebels]] during the [[Clone Wars]]. It was located in [[Sector S-29]] on the [[Inner Rim Territories|Inner Rim]] [[jungle]] [[planet]] [[Onderon]]. The camp lay amidst the [[jungle]] and was raised in the ruins of an ancient structure.<ref name="A War on Two Fronts Episode Guide">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/a-war-on-two-fronts-episode-guide|text="A War on Two Fronts" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref>

After the end of the Clone Wars and the [[Proclamation of the New Order|rise]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], [[Saw Gerrera]] and the [[Partisans]] maintained the camp. Shortly after the Empire's rise, [[Clone Force 99]] was [[Mission to Onderon (Clone Force 99)|sent]] to wipe out Gerrera's camp. However, due to [[Clone Sergeant]] [[Hunter]]'s reluctance to fire upon the unarmed civilians within the Partisans, the [[clone commando]] [[squad]] failed their mission.<ref name="Aftermath" /> Later, a newly founded [[Elite Squad]] led by former Clone Force 99 member [[Clone Commander]] [[Crosshair]], was [[Mission to Onderon (Elite Squad)|dispatched]] to once again attempt to eliminate the camp. By this [[time]], Partisan leader [[Saw Gerrera]] had already left the camp, leaving only a few of his [[soldier]]s and civilians behind.<ref name="Replacements" />

